<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Sekimura et al. (2015) Gierer–Meinhardt wing-cell focus at λ_c = 1.507 mm (Bicyclus anynana (Squinting Bush Brown))",
        "Sekimura et al. (2015) Gierer–Meinhardt wing-cell focus at λ_c = 1.507 mm faithfully reproduces Bicyclus anynana (Squinting Bush Brown) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bicyclus anynana (Squinting Bush Brown) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Bicyclus anynana (Squinting Bush Brown)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A cryptographic nanopublication signature. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.",
        "does_not_claim: A fossil predecessor or successor species. The chronoseries is the single Holocene terminus.",
        "does_not_claim: That the activator radial profile reproduces the black-gold pigment luminance (measured Pearson r = 0.26).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Adult GIF composites measured annulus colours onto ocelli whose positions come from specimen segmentation.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Explicit finite-difference integration of Eq. 3.1 and the dispersion identity σ(k).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Physical anchor λ_c = 1.507 mm, the scale assigned to this Holocene slot.",
        "reported_in_source: Eq. 3.1–3.2 and Table 1 of Sekimura et al. 2015: Gierer–Meinhardt kinetics, vein Dirichlet value 2 a1_ss, proximal Dirichlet k_p a1_ss, zero-flux inhibitor.",
        "reported_in_source: Focus number increases with anterior–posterior cell width (their S1 Appendix).",
        "reported_in_source: Low proximal activator selects a focus; high proximal activator suppresses it (their Fig. 4).",
        "transfer_boundary: Table 1 is dimensionless. Mapping λ_dim onto 1.507 mm is this slot's scale anchor, not a length reported in the 2015 paper.",
        "transfer_boundary: The photograph's leaf and wing-scale texture are the specimen, not a prediction of the wing-cell PDE." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/bicyclus_anynana_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Bicyclus anynana (Squinting Bush Brown); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Eq. 3.1–3.2 and Table 1 of Sekimura et al. 2015: Gierer–Meinhardt kinetics, vein Dirichlet value 2 a1_ss, proximal Dirichlet k_p a1_ss, zero-flux inhibitor. | Low proximal activator selects a focus; high proximal activator suppresses it (their Fig. 4). | Focus number increases with anterior–posterior cell width (their S1 Appendix).; reconstructed_in_script: Explicit finite-difference integration of Eq. 3.1 and the dispersion identity σ(k). | Physical anchor λ_c = 1.507 mm, the scale assigned to this Holocene slot. | Adult GIF composites measured annulus colours onto ocelli whose positions come from specimen segmentation.; transfer_boundary: Table 1 is dimensionless. Mapping λ_dim onto 1.507 mm is this slot's scale anchor, not a length reported in the 2015 paper. | The photograph's leaf and wing-scale texture are the specimen, not a prediction of the wing-cell PDE.; does_not_claim: That the activator radial profile reproduces the black-gold pigment luminance (measured Pearson r = 0.26). | A fossil predecessor or successor species. The chronoseries is the single Holocene terminus. | A cryptographic nanopublication signature. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.]; phenomenon_size: 9.6 cm (0.0963 m, log10=-1.016 m, tier=7_organism_cm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 9.6 cm to 9.6 cm): 9.6 cm:butterfly-eyespot-focus-rings" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.169367>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0141434> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bicyclus-anynana-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
